message.content:
Below is a minimal example of a “rotating card” that spins (or flips) when you hover over it.  
Feel free to copy‑paste the code into an `.html` file and open it in a browser.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card Demo</title>
<style>
/* ---------- 1️⃣ Basic reset & layout ---------- */
body {
    display:flex;
    justify-content:center;
    align-items:center;
    min-height:100vh;
    margin:0;
    background:#f0f0f0;
    font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;
}

/* ---------- 2️⃣ Card container ---------- */
.card {
    width:260px;
    height:360px;
    perspective:800px;          /* Gives depth to the 3D transform */
    cursor:pointer;
}

/* ---------- 3️⃣ Card inner wrapper (the part that actually rotates) ---------- */
.card-inner {
    position:relative;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    transition:transform 0.6s ease;   /* Smooth animation */
    transform-style:preserve-3d;      /* Needed for 3D children */
}

/* ---------- 4️⃣ Front & back faces ---------- */
.card-front,
.card-back {
    position:absolute;
    width:100%;
    height:100%;
    backface-visibility:hidden;       /* Hide the back face when turned */
    border-radius:12px;
    overflow:hidden;
    box-shadow:0 4px 10px rgba(0,0,0,.15);
}

.card-front {
    background:#fff;
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

.card-back {
    background:#fafafa;
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* Start rotated so it's hidden */
    display:flex;
    flex-direction:column;
    align-items:center;
    justify-content:center;
    padding:20px;
    text-align:center;
}

/* ---------- 5️⃣ Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover .card-inner {
    transform:rotateY(180deg);        /* Flip the card on hover */
}

/* ---------- 6️⃣ Optional styling for content ---------- */
.card h2 {
    margin:0 0 10px;
    font-size:1.4rem;
    color:#333;
}
.card p {
    margin:0;
    color:#666;
}
.card img {
    max-width:80%;
    border-radius:8px;
    margin-bottom:15px;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card">
    <div class="card-inner">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="card-front">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150?random=1" alt="Front Image">
            <h2>Front Title</h2>
            <p>This is the front side of the card.</p>
        </div>
        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="card-back">
            <img src="https://picsum.photos/200/150?random=2" alt="Back Image">
            <h2>Back Title</h2>
            <p>This is the back side of the card.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Step | What happens | Why |
|------|--------------|-----|
| **1** | `perspective` on `.card` | Gives the 3D effect; without it the rotation would look flat. |
| **2** | `.card-inner` has `transform-style: preserve-3d` | Allows its children (`.card-front`, `.card-back`) to maintain 3D positioning. |
| **3** | `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| **4** | `.card-back` starts rotated 180° | So it’s initially hidden behind the front. |
| **5** | On hover, `.card-inner` rotates 180° | Flips the whole card, revealing the back face. |

Feel free to tweak the dimensions, colors, or add more content. If you want a different rotation axis (e.g., flip vertically), change `rotateY` to `rotateX`. Enjoy!
